CBS will broadcast this year's Kennedy Center Honors , which will be held offsite amid the closure of the main facility.

The network's rights deal for the ceremony expired last year, and is said to have signed a one-year agreement for this year's ceremony. CBS has broadcast the honors since it started in 1978.

The ceremony will be held on Dec. 7 at Capital One Arena, but CBS will air the ceremony on Dec. 27. It also will stream live on Paramount+ Premium.

The ceremony will honor Paul Anka, David Foster, Andy Garcia, David Mamet and Barbara Mandrell. The ceremony will be produced by Den of Thieves, with Jesse Ignjatovic and Evan Prager as executive producers and Barb Bialkowski executive producer and showrunner. Micah Bickham will direct, and Cheche Alara will serve as music producer and music director. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

